<Page title="Privacy Policy" description="Allemojipedia privacy policy: no accounts, what is stored in your browser, how Google AdSense uses cookies, and how to control ad personalization." path="/privacy/" keywords={["privacy policy", "allemojipedia privacy"]} heading="Privacy policy" lead="Short version: there are no accounts, we do not collect personal information ourselves, and ads are served by Google.">
  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>Allemojipedia has no sign-up, no comments and no forms that send personal data to us. We do not run our own analytics or tracking scripts. If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you choose to write, and we use it only to reply.</p>

  <h2>Data stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/flag-emoji-quiz/">flag emoji quiz</a> saves your best score in your browser's local storage so it can show it to you next time. That value never leaves your device and you can erase it by clearing site data in your browser. Search runs entirely in your browser; what you type is not sent to us.</p>

  <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical request data such as IP address, browser type and the page requested, to deliver pages and protect against abuse. See Cloudflare's privacy policy for details.</p>

  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>We use Google AdSense to show ads. Google and its partners may use cookies or similar technologies to serve ads based on your visits to this and other websites.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>You can opt out of personalized advertising in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google's Ads Settings</a>.</li>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a> explains what is collected.</li>
    <li>Visitors in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland are shown a consent message by Google where required, and can change their choice at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third-party resources</h2>
  <p>On devices that cannot display flag emojis (mainly Windows), the flag quiz loads open-source flag images from the jsDelivr content delivery network. Loading those images sends a standard web request to jsDelivr.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is a general reference and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal data. Because we do not hold accounts or profiles, the only personal data we may have is email correspondence. To request its deletion, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the date below will be updated.</p>
</Page>
